From: Romain Tisserand <romain.tisserand@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AYANEO Pocket S: Add EFI boot compatibility

Under an EFI boot the ASoC card long name is built from DMI
(vendor-product-), and ucm.conf only matches conf.d/<driver>/<longname>.conf
or <driver>.conf, never the short card name "SM8550-APS". The other
AYANEO Pockets get these links from ROCKNIX; the Pocket S family has none.

The names below follow the "ayaneo-AYANEOPocketACE-" pattern and are a
best guess: check /proc/asound/cards on the device and fix if needed.

diff --git a/ucm2/conf.d/sm8550/ayaneo-AYANEOPocketS-.conf b/ucm2/conf.d/sm8550/ayaneo-AYANEOPocketS-.conf
new file mode 120000
index 0000000..414976a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ucm2/conf.d/sm8550/ayaneo-AYANEOPocketS-.conf
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+../../AYANEO/Pocket/AYANEO-Pocket.conf
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/ucm2/conf.d/sm8550/ayaneo-AYANEOPocketS1K-.conf b/ucm2/conf.d/sm8550/ayaneo-AYANEOPocketS1K-.conf
new file mode 120000
index 0000000..414976a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ucm2/conf.d/sm8550/ayaneo-AYANEOPocketS1K-.conf
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+../../AYANEO/Pocket/AYANEO-Pocket.conf
\ No newline at end of file
